ing it you know what i say  your president understands because  there's a teacher in the white house yes  yes  you certainly have his ear yeah and what  what is your message to him  well i think i go home every single day  and tell him about my students about  teachers  about what we're facing in our  classrooms and the thing i love about  joe is he listens and he has listened  and look at the american rescue plan and  look at all the money he gave to schools  and  and for  social development and mental health  things that are really important to  teachers  and  i knew he would be a great education  president and that's one of the reasons  i was out there campaigning my heart out  well the teachers who are sitting here  what what frustrations do you have the  nature of teaching has somewhat changed  we are taking on many more roles than  than before there are students who need  you know mental health services or who  might  be lacking with their social emotional  development because of the pandemic and  we have to be  in some ways counselors i teach in a  school  in the most beautiful community shout  out meadowlark elementary  and  a lot of the kids did not have access to  the kinds of privileges that my children  will have access to  and and making sure that i was  not failing as a teacher at the same  time i was trying to not fail as a  father was  difficult to to go to bed with every  night and and it filled me with guilt  teacher guilt has been around since as  long as there have been teachers teacher  guilt teacher guilt that that feeling  like i'm not doing enough and we are  carrying all of the pre-pandemic weight  on our shoulders  and then all of this new stuff and  you know in a lot of ways we're stronger  we can bear more weight than we could  before dr biden what has frustrated you  during this time during this pandemic  well i guess you know not being able to  be in the classroom like everybody else  to see our students in person do you  ever come home